# Normalize all text files to LF in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# `eol=lf` (rather than bare `text=auto`) is deliberate: Git for Windows ships
# `core.autocrlf=true` in its system config, which would otherwise rewrite
# checkouts to CRLF and re-dirty the tree on every machine. Pinning the working
# tree to LF keeps Windows, the Lovable Linux sandbox, and CI byte-identical.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never line-ending converted, never textually merged.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Generated files: keep them out of review diffs, but still mergeable.
# Deliberately NOT marked `binary`/`merge=binary` — that would make every
# conflict unresolvable instead of merely noisy. On conflict, regenerate.
bun.lock             -diff linguist-generated=true
src/routeTree.gen.ts -diff linguist-generated=true
